SM(627,{"n":"Revelation 14.8-20","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Revelation 14.8-20.mp3","d":2487.4,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.96,"Saying Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city, because she has made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication."],[34.56,"There's a uh there's an image."],[37.89,"And it's alluding to imagery that, as we mentioned a little while ago before we started recording, we're gonna get into it in chapter 17."],[47.49,"You see how St."],[48.21,"John likes introduces these things, and then remember he mentioned the beast before he talked about the beasts."],[57.17,"This is the same thing."],[58.05,"We're gonna find out more about uh Babylon, what city that is, why it's a she."],[67.85,"And uh just drinking of the wine of the wrath of her fornication."],[71.85,"But spoilers um uh Babylon, the Babylonian Empire was the first major world empire, the original Babylonian Empire."],[84.49,"Not the Nebuchadnezzar, that we think of the Babylonians of the Old Testament."],[88.27,"That's the Neo-Babylonian Empire."],[91.47,"So the Babylonian Empire is mid second millennium BC."],[98.91,"Um, and that's really the first empire in terms of uh I mean, there are always kings who would sort of make the kings of neighboring cities their vassals and that kind of thing."],[103.55,"'re But when we talking about the uh the Martu who set up the first Babylonian Empire in the city of Babylon, like Hammurabi being the most famous one, who are the biblical Amorites."],[126.15,"Hammurabi, for example, uh got his sandals imported from Crete."],[135.91,"Hammurabi in Babylon uh was forging things out of bronze."],[140.95,"This is why it's called the Bronze Age."],[142.39,"He was getting the copper from Cyprus and the tin from what's now Afghanistan."],[148.44,"So this is empire"],[152.88,"This is a world, an old world empire."],[157.14,"That's and economically dominating, politically dominating the world."],[163.32,"And the Bronze Age collapse happens and it all falls apart."],[167.08,"And the story of the Tower of Babel in Genesis 11 is really a very condensed version of the rise and fall of the Babylonian Empire."],[176.36,"That's why it's the Tower of Babel."],[179.0,"Babylon And so as an image functions sort of like the beast from the sea."],[188.34,"In that it's not just referring to that city in particular, which was kind of in ruins at this point."],[194.4,"It's it's not just referring to that empire, but it becomes symbolic of, you know, what St."],[199.6,"Augustine would call the city of man."],[201.45,"The as opposed to the city of God."],[203.55,"Like world empire as such."],[207.68,"And so part of this last judgment is that this sort of imperial world power opposed to God is now destroyed."],[219.28,"Which is, as we'll see when this gets developed more in chapter 17, really bad news for all the people who are worshipping it."],[228.42,"That's the fact that it's now wiped out."],[231.7,"The play, the thing you were putting all your hope and all your trust in."],[233.94,"But this again isn't just something that happens at the end of time"],[240.03,"Because remember, part and parcel of Daniel's vision."],[245.59,"Of the succession of empires with the different beasts who all get sort of congealed here is that there's a succession."],[253.45,"There's one after the other."],[257.53,"And they all rise and they all fall."],[261.47,"Which makes it very different than God."],[264.72,"The true God."],[266.32,"But which also means anyone who is putting their trust and their hope in them."],[273.7,"Is uh going to be left out."],[274.58,"uh I'm trying to remember who it was who said, he who weds himself to the spirit of the age soon finds himself a widower."],[288.14,"Uh but that's what that's what happens."],[294.31,"The people who put their trust in the Assyrian Empire and the Assyrian gods."],[299.75,"I would say left out in the cold, but they were mostly left dead when the Babylonians showed up."],[304.76,"And guess what happened to the Babylonians when the Persians showed up?"],[309.0,"Guess what happened to the Persians when Alexander the Great showed up?"],[312.68,"I guess what happened to Alexander the Great's successors when the Romans showed up."],[318.58,"And on and on and on."],[320.44,"And so more spoilers for chapter 17."],[323.4,"Uh uh, this'll this this should lose some listeners."],[328.28,"Uh the the the current embodiment of this imperial power is the United States of America."],[334.44,"Hasn't been for very long."],[335.72,"It was Britain until World War II."],[337.96,"But uh now it's us, and guess what?"],[340.84,"I don't even think in that much time it's not gonna be anymore."],[348.09,"So putting your trust put put not your trust in princes and sons of men in whom there is no salvation."],[353.7,"That includes presidents, that includes prime ministers, that includes kings and queens, that includes everybody."],[361.14,"Because it's one after the other"],[364.14,"And they're all glorious."],[366.4,"You go and look at the art of the British Empire."],[370.86,"The depictions of Britannia."],[373.04,"And the the sun never sets upon the British."],[376.38,"And you look at some of the horrors that were involved in that in various places."],[381.79,"But ultimately it all comes crumbling down."],[386.43,"And there's as much blood on the way out as there was on the way in."],[391.39,"Just roles tend to get reversed."],[395.31,"So, yeah, so this also, this statement also is good news for some people and bad news for some other people."],[404.95,"For all the people whose hope and trust was in this world and its system."],[410.29,"This is very bad news."],[413.01,"For the 144,000."],[414.71,"For those who weren't part of it."],[417.16,"This is great news."],[418.84,"This is deliverance."],[421.37,"When this happens."],[434.53,"We've talked before about how uh when you see of in an English translation of the New Testament, it's a punt."],[441.25,"Uh, it means there was a Greek genitive word, which could be translated, interpreted in a whole bunch of different ways."],[447.53,"Or you could just say of the be noncommittal"],[453.81,"Um the connection here is that the wine of her fornication, meaning that the wine represents her fornication."],[465.74,"So the idea is that the people who are sort of worshiping and serving Babylon and this system were fornicating with her, is the idea."],[476.86,"So it's comparing that to sexual immorality, which was a common image in the Old Testament."],[484.74,"When God comes and reproaches Israel because they've been following after the gods of the other nations and right and that kind of thing."],[491.34,"and He compares it to, you know, I was your husband and you went out fornicated."],[498.74,"So that's that's picking up that same imagery."],[502.47,"Um then the wrath, is not like her wrath against these other these other people."],[513.49,"It's the wrath engendered by her fornication."],[517.17,"So by participating in this fornication, they brought this wrath upon themselves."],[522.87,"And what is wrath?"],[524.15,"Wrath is being on the wrong end of that correction."],[528.73,"It's wrath is when you start out as first and you end up as last."],[533.54,"That's loss, suffering, wrath"],[543.43,"Verse 9. Then a third angel followed them, saying with a loud voice, If anyone worships the beast and his image and receives his mark on his forehead or on his hand, he himself shall also drink of the wine of the wrath of God, which is poured out full strength into the cup of his indignation."],[564.47,"That full strength means not mingled with water, is the analogy."],[568.07,"So it's just straight."],[571.99,"He shall be tormented with fire and brimstone in the presence of the holy angels and in the presence of the Lamb."],[577.43,"We'll pause there before we get to verse 11"],[585.47,"So again, this is sort of expanding on that imagery regarding Babylon."],[594.53,"So if you're one of the followers of the beast, one of the worshippers of the beast who gets his mark instead of right gods."],[604.71,"Then you're also going to."],[607.25,"This is saying, I'm talking about you."],[611.25,"This isn't just the other world leaders or the rich or the power."],[615.02,"If you're a part of this is this is you."],[618.54,"And notice. it doesn't say they're gonna be tormented in hell"],[626.72,"They're gonna go and get sent and get flogged by demons or something."],[630.9,"Stabbed with a pitchfork."],[632.95,"It says that they're gonna be tormented with fire and brimstone in the presence of the holy angels and in the presence of the Lamb."],[642.21,"Well, what does that mean?"],[643.73,"Well, what happens to someone who is unrepentantly wicked."],[651.53,"In the Old Testament, say, when they walk into the tabernacle."],[655.69,"Where they touch the Ark of the Covenant."],[658.53,"Yeah. And specifically, like if you look at Nadab and Abuhu, everybody's two favorite biblical characters."],[667.13,"Who are the sons of Aaron who go into the tabernacle drunk at the wrong time to offer incense."],[672.75,"It says fire comes out from the presence."],[676.85,"The presence of the Lamb here."],[678.53,"From the presence of the Lord, from the presence of Yahweh, and consume them."],[685.73,"So, as we've talked about a lot when we're talking about the Torah and how it worked, to come into the presence of God as wicked."],[696.59,"Unrepentant. Sinful, rebellious, hardened in our rebellion and hatred of God."],[703.25,"Is this horrible experience that's described all through the Old Testament in these fire terms that get picked up again here?"],[711.71,"They're going to come into the presence of the Lamb, and contra to the people we're just talking about, like the 144,000, who have nothing to fear when they come into the presence of Christ."],[723.33,"For these people, that's a profoundly fearsome and terrible experience."],[729.46,"Why? Because he hates them?"],[730.98,"No, because they hate him."],[735.08,"Because they hate him."],[737.56,"So Hebrews uses this language that our God is a consuming fire."],[741.8,"That fire image is used by the Old Testament prophets in two ways."],[747.01,"We approach God and we come into the fire of his holiness."],[752.73,"And when that happens, one of two things happens."],[756.17,"Either that fire purifies us."],[761.45,"Because none of us show up totally pure."],[765.53,"But that fire either purifies us."],[768.09,"They usually use images of metal being refined in a fire."],[772.25,"All the impurities get burned away, and all you have left is the pure precious metal."],[777.29,"Or we're consumed."],[780.41,"If all we are is impurities."],[784.38,"We're consumed. That's the imagery they use."],[786.7,"So that's the same imagery here."],[788.94,"Because what did the first angel say?"],[790.78,"Get ready. God's coming"],[792.1,"And for these people, this is this profound, wonderful promise"],[799.27,"For you, if you're one of these people, it's gonna be really bad."],[803.85,"But notice it isn't St."],[805.69,"John seeing this happen."],[807.77,"It's an angel proclaiming this as a warning to those people."],[815.03,"Before, I mean, immediately before it happens, but before it happens."],[818.24,"And just like what the other angels said, this isn't just one thing for one day in the future."],[823.76,"This is a thing for every day."],[827.28,"And so St"],[829.09,"John is asking the question to his readers, in our modern language how, much of you sold out?"],[838.05,"Because a fair number of St."],[840.93,"John's readers were striving hard to follow Christ and suffering."],[845.89,"But there were also people among the original people who heard this who weren't really trying so hard, and maybe because of that weren't suffering so much."],[857.27,"Who were trying to straddle the fence."],[859.44,"Keep one foot in the Roman system and one foot the church."],[866.34,"And when the chips were down, sometimes maybe they say Christian, maybe sometimes they didn't."],[874.56,"Depending on what the stakes were, an immediate decision."],[876.16,"And so this warning is addressed to them"],[883.21,"Right. Have you been participant?"],[887.53,"Because remember, this image of the mark was connected to participating in the commerce, in the in the day-to-day things of this world."],[899.53,"And this is given again as a warning."],[902.59,"Because if you're reading this or you're hearing this, it's not too late for you."],[913.15,"Verse 11: And the smoke of their torment ascends forever and ever, and they have no rest day or night, who worship the beast. in his image, and whoever receives the mark of his name"],[926.55,"Notice. So we have this, this is ongoing forever, but notice that verb who worship the beast in his image."],[935.84,"It's actually a participle, but that's it's a verbal noun."],[941.12,"Um that's present tense."],[949.52,"It's not those who worshipped."],[953.2,"Like you did this, so now you're doomed."],[955.84,"You did this, so now you're being punished."],[961.09,"So even in this torment, that's being described, they continue to follow the beast's image."],[971.01,"So again, this is unrepentant."],[975.33,"This is unrepentant evil."],[977.49,"And so, as long as their lack of repentance is ongoing, so is their suffering."],[992.23,"Okay. So verse 12, here is the patience of the saints."],[997.99,"Here are those who keep the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus."],[1004.47,"Um, here is the patience of the saints."],[1010.43,"Sounds weird. But that's essentially an introductory thing of I'm about to describe, why it is that the saints are able to be patient."],[1024.27,"He's using patient because again, think about the martyrs."],[1027.41,"How long, O Lord?"],[1029.59,"Will you allow this to go on?"],[1031.75,"Um, and then he defines what he means by saints, what he means by holy ones."],[1038.32,"Because that word is used, for example, to describe angels."],[1041.84,"Um the ones he's talking about here are those who keep the commandments of God."],[1047.44,"Okay, and then we have this it's translated, and the faith of Jesus."],[1052.04,"So first of all, you have a a horrible of punt there."],[1056.46,"The faith of Jesus."],[1057.58,"What does that mean?"],[1059.02,"Jesus had faith, and they have the same faith."],[1065.87,"So, as we've talked about a bunch of times before, the word faith is translated faith, and sometimes believe, it's the same word or belief, uh, is better translated faithfulness."],[1080.08,"And so this should be like the faith faithfulness to Christ."],[1088.21,"Faithfulness related to Christ."],[1091.29,"And that's parallel to back there, these are the ones who follow the Lamb wherever he goes."],[1098.74,"That idea of faithfulness."],[1104.18,"But so notice also the prominence there that it's actually mentioned first keeping the commandments."],[1113.46,"So this may be a no offense."],[1117.46,"But this may be a sorry to our Protestant friends."],[1120.58,"That in addition to faith, we see keeping the commandments listed here."],[1124.26,"It's almost like faith is not alone or all by itself."],[1127.66,"Um but also that faithfulness consists of something."],[1136.27,"So this is this is not saying those who keep the commandments and who have the right ideas in their heads."],[1144.75,"Just bluntly it isn't."],[1146.91,"And and Protestants don't have to believe that."],[1149.39,"I'm not I'm not trying to caricature."],[1151.73,"Um but um but I take my digs once a while."],[1156.13,"But um the the the the faithfulness consists, these are not like two radically different things."],[1162.99,"Like you could do one and not the other."],[1167.63,"Keeping the commandments of God is being faithful to Christ."],[1170.83,"And being faithful to Christ means that you will keep the commandments of God."],[1174.37,"You can't have one of those without without the other one."],[1177.65,"So that's what he's talking about."],[1178.45,"And those people, they're able to be patient, meaning literally long-suffering"],[1186.89,"They're able to remain faithful and keep the answer despite suffering."],[1191.45,"Why? Here we go, verse 13."],[1194.73,"Then I heard a voice from heaven saying to me, Write, blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from now on."],[1202.97,"Yes, says the Spirit, that they may rest from their labors and their works follow them."],[1215.73,"Here's another place where this is clearly not talking about the distant future."],[1221.18,"If you die now, oh man."],[1224.66,"If I just died, you know, right before Christ returned."],[1230.87,"Then I'd be blessed."],[1232.15,"But now. So from now on, isn't even really I mean it is from when St."],[1239.24,"John is having the vision, but really it's from uh Christ's resurrection."],[1246.78,"Which wasn't that long ago that St."],[1248.46,"John is writing this."],[1249.34,"It's decades, but not that long."],[1251.74,"Um so that's that blessed are those who die from now on."],[1257.0,"Why? Why? And remember, this is why the saints are able to do endure suffering in this life."],[1265.09,"And remain faithful."],[1266.77,"Because when they die on this earth, they rest from their labors."],[1273.48,"So they rest from that suffering."],[1275.24,"That suffering is over."],[1276.94,"All of that is over."],[1278.22,"And their works follow them."],[1281.18,"But what they did in this life."],[1284.83,"And being faithful to Christ and keeping the commandments, that endures."],[1292.11,"So when someone who's a follower of Christ dies in this world, there are things that end, and there are things that don't end."],[1305.24,"The love that they shared with people does not end."],[1307.48,"That follows after them"],[1312.17,"The goodness, the peace."],[1314.78,"The person they became in Christ."],[1317.42,"That all follows them."],[1318.7,"That all endures forever."],[1320.54,"But things like suffering, pain, sin, weakness, struggling, that dies."],[1327.9,"That's over. And so we could say that that person is blessed."],[1336.3,"That person is blessed, no matter how they died."],[1339.5,"Whether they were tortured to death by the Romans, whether they died in an old age, in their sleep."],[1345.88,"However it was."],[1348.14,"If they're a follower of Christ, they're blessed."],[1351.7,"Doesn't matter how old or how young they were."],[1356.38,"That's a radical thing."],[1360.86,"In the ancient world, the blessed person is the one who had a long life, and no bad things happen to them."],[1370.38,"Aristotle wrote and wrote and wrote about this."],[1373.66,"Read the Nicomachean ethics, the Eudeman ethics."],[1376.72,"It's all about how do you live a happy life?"],[1381.84,"Is it even within your power?"],[1383.36,"Because isn't there fortune involved?"],[1386.72,"Some people just have bad fortune and suffer a lot."],[1389.92,"They can't really be said to be happy."],[1391.98,"And how does virtue play to it?"],[1394.58,"All these things."],[1395.4,"But a person who dies young, a person who's tortured to death, a person who lives in poverty, this is not the blessed person."],[1406.22,"This is not the blessed person in the ancient world."],[1418.51,"Is not going to be long suffering in the way that Christians were."],[1424.51,"If you went and tortured them and said, I want you, you know, if you went and tortured a pagan Syrian and said, I want you to deny Baal and worship Jupiter, he'd be like, sure."],[1435.61,"No skin off of my nose, they're probably the same dude anyway."],[1439.38,"So there was not someone."],[1443.67,"But so this is why the saints can because they know that whatever happens."],[1448.52,"What's the worst thing that can happen to you in this world in this life?"],[1452.2,"You could die a horrible death."],[1453.49,"I mean, that's pretty much the worst thing that could happen."],[1457.94,"And if that puts you into this blessed state, if that becomes a hope instead of something you're afraid of."],[1466.19,"Then you're truly blessed in this life."],[1468.63,"Because then you really have nothing to fear."],[1472.41,"This is where that saying, no one can harm the righteous man comes from."],[1477.65,"Because even if you kill him."],[1480.66,"You only put an end to all the bad things that he's had to struggle with and deal with."],[1486.19,"And all the good follows him."],[1491.87,"Verse 14. Then I looked, and behold, a white cloud, and on the cloud sat one like the Son of Man, having on his head a golden crown, and in his hand a sharp sickle."],[1510.67,"So this imagery is again straight out of the book of Daniel."],[1515.95,"Is this starting in a new sign?"],[1518.19,"No, not yet."],[1519.15,"We're coming up to the end, though"],[1525.83,"But so in Daniel, there's this story, when we loop around and get to Daniel in a few years."],[1533.75,"We'll go over it more detail."],[1535.59,"But it's actually kind of a remix of the enthronement of Baal, actually."],[1539.11,"But where Daniel sees the Ancient of Days and then he sees one like a son of man, which originally meant someone who looks human."],[1547.61,"Essentially. So what looked like a human, but riding on clouds come up before him."],[1553.85,"And he's then given authority and power."],[1556.94,"And so uh St."],[1558.86,"John is using this imagery and expanding on this."],[1562.44,"But so that that that riding the clouds language, doesn't maybe impress us much."],[1571.42,"Um, but um this was imagery that was used of like Baal."],[1578.78,"Baal was the cloud rider, that was one of his titles, because he was a storm god, and so this was a symbol of like divinity and power, and that imagery gets applied to Yahweh, the God of Israel, in several psalms and in other places."],[1597.26,"One of them we read tonight at Vespers."],[1600.36,"He walketh upon the wings, he makes the clouds his chariot, he walks on the wings of the wind."],[1605.69,"So what's being juxtaposed here in Daniel is this looks like a human."],[1613.59,"This looks like a human, but he's riding the clouds of heaven, which is a mark of divinity."],[1622.28,"And so this figure of the Son of Man in Second Temple, sort of Jewish literature, pre Christian Jewish literature, is sort of this apocalyptic figure."],[1634.04,"And gets connected very quickly."],[1635.8,"I mean, even in the book of Enoch, first Enoch, third century BC, gets connected to the Messiah."],[1642.45,"As this sort of divine Messiah figure."],[1646.37,"And he's going to come on the clouds of heaven to judge."],[1649.41,"And Christ himself refers to this several times in the Gospel, especially in St"],[1655.51,"Matthew's Gospel. He uses the title Son of Man for Himself all over the place."],[1660.73,"Connecting himself to this figure."],[1662.81,"But this specific imagery in St."],[1666.01,"Matthew's Gospel and St."],[1667.21,"Mark's Gospel, he talks about, at one point, just straightforwardly, the same imagery St."],[1672.49,"John is using here."],[1673.29,"He says, when the Son of Man comes on the clouds of heaven with his holy angels to judge."],[1683.93,"But he also says to the high priest, when the high priest kind of quarters him and says, Alright, spill it, are you the Messiah?"],[1692.3,"U noh, he says, Are you the Son of God?"],[1695.44,"And Christ says to him, henceforth, you will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of heaven."],[1703.13,"That henceforth is really like, This is how next time you see me."],[1708.79,"This is what it's gonna be."],[1710.33,"And that's what the high priest says."],[1712.17,"We don't need any more witnesses."],[1713.77,"We've heard him blaspheme, right in front of us."],[1719.41,"So, so this is abundant what St."],[1723.81,"John is doing here would be abundantly clear, to his original Jewish readers that this is Christ, and this is now sort of the image of the Last Judgment."],[1732.22,"The sickle. You use it at the harvest."],[1733.76,"And when Christ is talking about the last judgment again, especially in St"],[1738.57,"Matthew's gospel, over and over again he uses these images of a harvest."],[1743.15,"You've got the wheat and the weeds."],[1745.25,"You've got the wheat and the chaff."],[1746.78,"This idea of harvest and separating."],[1748.46,"He was talking to farmers, which makes it a very right."],[1751.74,"And these people were subsistence farmers, so they knew about these kind of things."],[1756.06,"So it was a very helpful metaphor for them."],[1758.14,"But that same metaphor is being picked up here by Saint John."],[1761.02,"So he's coming now with this sickle to judge, meaning to separate out."],[1771.47,"Verse 15, and another angel came out of the temple crying with a loud voice to him who sat on the cloud, thrust in your sickle and reap, for the time has come for you to reap, for the harvest of the earth is ripe."],[1786.63,"So he who sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth, and the earth was reaped."],[1793.35,"So where's this temple?"],[1795.51,"So we've talked about it's in heaven."],[1798.39,"I thought they were on science."],[1800.61,"But there is no temple there right now."],[1802.53,"That's where the Lamb was."],[1803.97,"Yeah. But this is now coming on the clouds of heaven."],[1807.05,"We went back, remember there was the angel in the midst of heaven, so we've gone back to heaven."],[1811.42,"So this is the heavenly sanctuary."],[1815.2,"And so now's the time."],[1817.46,"This is another piece of imagery, again, picking up on what Christ used, that for a time."],[1823.6,"The wheat and the weeds are allowed to grow together."],[1826.8,"Because you don't want to go and try and get rid of the weeds because you might kill all the wheat."],[1831.06,"In the process."],[1832.98,"The time comes where you've got a harvest where these things get separated out."],[1838.74,"So there's people using the language he's been using."],[1842.18,"There's people marked by God, and people with the mark of the beast."],[1847.06,"They're all living together."],[1849.9,"Things aren't necessarily going well for the people with the mark of God, but they're all living together."],[1855.02,"So now's the time where things are going to be set right."],[1859.5,"This is going to be separated out."],[1861.26,"Harvest begins And so he thrusts the sickle in."],[1867.4,"Verse 17. Then another angel came out of the temple, which is in heaven."],[1872.12,"Make it explicit there."],[1873.96,"He also having a sharp sickle."],[1876.52,"And another angel came out from the altar who had power over fire."],[1881.0,"And he cried with a loud cry to him who had the sharp sickle, saying, Thrust in your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of the vine of the earth, for her grapes are fully ripe."],[1898.2,"This is where the title of Grapes of Wrath came from, actually."],[1902.2,"But um, so we've gotta, it's right."],[1906.04,"a There's time known only to God when judgment happens."],[1907.2,"This is the time."],[1908.64,"We've talked before about the last judgment."],[1916.4,"God gives time for repentance because he wills that none should perish."],[1921.76,"But he also won't let evil take place forever."],[1926.24,"And so there's a time known only to him, whereas we see in the scriptures in the life of the whole world, in terms of the final judgment in Christ's return, in terms of any given nation or people group, in terms of any individual person, where the need to put an end to evil in God's sight outweighs giving more time to repent and that's the point at which that person leaves this world right that nation or group is judged right when the whole earth will ultimately be set right why is it always related to wine because when it talks about wrath when it talks about wrath yeah is it is it just because of like being drunk on power or something or is it like drunkenness um and uh wine especially unmingled wine."],[1983.16,"Meaning without water."],[1985.58,"Not watered down, straight, pure, it's sort of biting, burning, caustic."],[1992.62,"Take a shot at whiskey."],[1994.18,"right The ancient world wine was the main thing you drank,?"],[1999.48,"Well, there's always all this mix."],[2001.16,"Yeah. Yeah, you would cut it."],[2003.93,"So it's so potent it's almost like poison."],[2007.53,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[2010.17,"And it's there's that burning right element of it."],[2015.77,"And also there's a connection with the there's a Hebrew idiom for wine, where wine is called the blood of grapes."],[2028.41,"So there's sort of a blood connection right there, too."],[2034.49,"Um that I think factors in there."],[2037.05,"Verse 19 So the angel thrust his sickle into the earth and gathered the vine of the earth and threw it into the great wine press of the wrath of God."],[2050.13,"Uh so conjure the battle hymn of the Republic."],[2055.81,"Uh this is not talking about the Union Army."],[2060.13,"I'm just gonna throw that out there."],[2063.01,"I am not pro-Confederate, even though I now live in Louisiana."],[2067.73,"But this is also not talking about the Union Army."],[2072.61,"Um the vintage where the grapes of wrath are stored, is what I'm referring to, which is referencing this."],[2081.73,"Yeah. Um the wine press was trampled outside the city, and blood came out of the wine press up to the horses' bridles for 1,600 furlongs."],[2096.39,"I think that they use furlongs."],[2100.87,"Oh, they did the math in the Orthodox Study Bible notes."],[2106.31,"184 miles. I'm sure it was definitely."],[2112.15,"Yes. Roughly. Give or take."],[2115.91,"At the size of a horse's bridle, so that deep for that far."],[2119.04,"So the idea is not we're supposed to get an exact measurement of this is exactly how much blood of grapes."],[2124.88,"So you see the blood."],[2126.32,"Right. The blood of grapes"],[2126.48,"The idea is it's a lot"],[2133.38,"It's not a little trickle."],[2135.0,"It's a torrent."],[2136.93,"It's a torrent."],[2139.09,"So is this just saying, hey man, you're gonna get squished."],[2145.55,"If you're if you don't get right."],[2153.68,"So this is actually picking up on sacrificial imagery."],[2160.08,"I know that's not immediately apparent to us."],[2163.44,"Okay. But this is part of why St."],[2166.8,"John invoked the temple in heaven."],[2170.76,"He's talking about this."],[2173.16,"We don't think about what the temple was actually like."],[2181.0,"Because and this is thankfully for me."],[2184.2,"I'm very happy to be a priest of the new covenant."],[2186.92,"I don't have to go around throwing blood."],[2189.08,"I don't have to butcher animals."],[2191.74,"I don't have to."],[2192.94,"There's lots of stuff I don't have to do."],[2195.18,"But at the temple, because there were constantly animal sacrifices going on, and because all the blood had to be drained and disposed of, there were these big gutters that were sort of full of blood and awful all the time."],[2212.38,"This is not an appealing image to us"],[2213.91,"Like coming out of the temple."],[2218.23,"The smell would be even less appealing, I'm sure."],[2222.07,"But so this was sort of the constant when sacrifices were going on."],[2227.71,"And so this imagery of this wine press, of God's wrath, from which all this blood is pouring, is applying sacrificial imagery to this."],[2246.93,"And this exact image is going to be developed again more in the next cycle in a few chapters."],[2253.01,"Because a new cycle actually starts the next chapter."],[2256.57,"In chapter 15, beginning of chapter 15."],[2258.81,"We're going to get another set of seven."],[2262.49,"But so this will be developed more, but this is pointing to the sacrificial image."],[2267.61,"And this imagery is used when the day of the Lord, the day of Yahweh, is talked about by the Old Testament prophets."],[2275.45,"They use this language of the Lord preparing his sacrifice."],[2286.93,"Literally, they use this descriptive language, the armies of the enemies of God and their horses."],[2296.34,"And those are all slaughtered and offered as a sacrifice, meaning offered as food to uh to uh the animals of creation the vultures, the buzzards, the beasts."],[2317.99,"All come and eat."],[2319.11,"God sort of puts on this banquet for the scavenger animals, the unclean animals."],[2326.65,"The sacrificial banquet of all of his enemies."],[2332.61,"So that's St."],[2335.17,"John is here at the end of this cycle, sort of dropping."],[2339.11,"The first beginning of that image."],[2341.43,"He's gonna develop it more. at the end of the next cycle when he comes back to it"],[2349.23,"And uh yeah, I won't tease that anymore."],[2353.95,"But we'll come back to that to that idea."],[2356.83,"But that's what's going on here with this huge torrent of great blood wine going on here."],[2365.63,"Is the idea that this has this has turned into this into this sacrifice."],[2373.23,"And that's that's a sort of inversion image that's common in other places too."],[2379.95,"There's a point in the Psalms, I can't remember the Psalm number off the top of my head, where it talks about um might be in Isaiah, not the Psalms."],[2389.03,"I'm drawing the blank."],[2390.71,"Need to wrap up."],[2391.59,"It's getting too late."],[2392.87,"Be more caffeine."],[2397.19,"But where it talks about God smashing the heads of Leviathan and giving it as food to the Ethiopians."],[2407.0,"It's the same kind of thing."],[2408.52,"Him taking this enemy."],[2411.02,"That represents chaos and death and destruction, and then not only defeating it, but then giving it as nourishment to his creation."],[2424.0,"And bringing life out of it."],[2429.6,"And so that's even true. of the wickedness in the world"],[2437.56,"This is an image of God taking all the wickedness in the world."],[2441.16,"It's come to this fruition and turning around and turning it into a sacrifice."],[2449.32,"Turning it into something that can give life."],[2454.68,"So, as I mentioned, we'll go ahead and stop here."],[2457.72,"We're at the end of a chapter."],[2458.84,"We're about to begin another cycle."],[2460.36,"So this is kind of a perfect spot."],[2462.04,"So thank you, everybody."],[2465.0,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2472.36,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2475.16,"unsel at ancient. That's wholecofaith.com"]],"o":[{"t":22.96,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:8 - Babylon is fallen","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Second angel: <b>\"Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city\"</b> - all nations drank <b>wine of the wrath of her fornication</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Image alluding to <b>chapter 17</b> - \"we're gonna get into it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">John's habit: introduces things, develops later - like <b>the beast</b> mentioned before <b>the beasts</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Coming: what city, <b>why it's a \"she\"</b>, the wine of wrath of her fornication</li></ul>"},{"t":71.85,"lv":3,"h":"Original Babylon: the first world empire","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Spoiler: <b>Babylonian Empire = first major world empire</b>, mid-<b>2nd millennium BC</b></li><li class=\"d0\">not Nebuchadnezzar's - that's the <b>Neo-Babylonian</b> Empire</li><li class=\"d0\">Earlier: kings making neighbouring city kings <b>vassals</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Martu</b> set up first Babylonian Empire in city of Babylon - <b>Hammurabi</b> most famous</li><li class=\"d0\">Martu = the biblical <b>Amorites</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Global economy: Hammurabi's <b>sandals imported from Crete</b></li><li class=\"d0\">forging <b>bronze</b> - copper from <b>Cyprus</b>, tin from what's now <b>Afghanistan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">= why \"<b>Bronze Age</b>\"; economically and politically dominating the world</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bronze Age collapse</b> → it all falls apart</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tower of Babel, Genesis 11</b> = condensed version of rise and fall of Babylonian Empire</li></ul>"},{"t":179.0,"lv":3,"h":"Babylon as symbol: the city of man","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Babylon as image works like <b>the beast from the sea</b></li><li class=\"d0\">not just that city (in ruins by now) or that empire</li><li class=\"d0\">becomes symbolic of <b>Augustine's \"city of man\"</b> vs <b>city of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>world empire as such</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Part of <b>last judgment</b>: imperial world power opposed to God <b>destroyed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">chapter 17 develops it - <b>really bad news</b> for all who worship it</li><li class=\"d0\">the thing you put <b>all your hope and trust in</b> wiped out</li></ul>"},{"t":233.94,"lv":2,"h":"Empires rise and fall - not just at the end","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not only end of time - recall <b>Daniel's vision</b>: <b>succession of empires</b>, beasts here \"congealed\"</li><li class=\"d0\">one after another: <b>all rise, all fall</b> - very different from the <b>true God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">anyone trusting in them is <b>left out</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Quote: <b>\"he who weds himself to the spirit of the age soon finds himself a widower\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Assyrian</b> Empire and gods → \"mostly left dead\" when <b>Babylonians</b> showed up</li><li class=\"d0\">Babylonians → <b>Persians</b> → <b>Alexander</b> → his successors → <b>Romans</b> … \"on and on\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Spoiler for 17: current embodiment of imperial power = <b>United States</b> - was <b>Britain</b> until WWII</li><li class=\"d0\">\"this should lose some listeners\"; won't last long either</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Psalm 146: \"put not your trust in princes\"</b> - presidents, prime ministers, kings, queens, everybody</li><li class=\"d0\">British Empire art: <b>Britannia</b>, \"sun never sets\" - glorious, but horrors; <b>as much blood on the way out as in</b> - \"roles get reversed\"</li></ul>"},{"t":395.31,"lv":2,"h":"Good news, bad news; \"wine of her fornication\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Fall of Babylon = <b>bad news</b> for those whose hope was in this world and its system</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Great news</b> for the <b>144,000</b> and those not part of it - <b>deliverance</b></li><li class=\"d0\">English <b>\"of\"</b> = a <b>punt</b> - Greek <b>genitive</b>, many possible readings</li><li class=\"d0\">here: wine <b>represents</b> her fornication</li><li class=\"d0\">those worshipping and serving Babylon's system = <b>fornicating with her</b></li><li class=\"d0\">sexual-immorality image common in OT - <b>God reproaching Israel</b> for following other nations' gods: \"I was your husband and you went out fornicated\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wrath</b> = not her wrath against others - wrath <b>engendered by her fornication</b></li><li class=\"d0\">by participating they <b>brought wrath on themselves</b></li><li class=\"d0\">What is wrath? <b>being on wrong end of correction</b> - \"start out first and end up last\"</li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>loss, suffering</b></li></ul>"},{"t":543.43,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:9-10 - Third angel: the mark","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Third angel</b>: anyone worshipping <b>beast and image</b>, receiving <b>mark</b> on forehead or hand → drinks <b>wine of God's wrath</b> poured <b>full strength</b> into the cup of his indignation</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>full strength</b> = <b>not mingled with water</b>; \"straight\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>tormented with fire and brimstone</b> in presence of <b>holy angels</b> and <b>the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Expands the Babylon imagery - if you're a <b>follower of the beast</b>, \"<b>I'm talking about you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">not just other world leaders, the rich, the powerful</li></ul>"},{"t":618.54,"lv":3,"h":"Fire in the presence of the Lamb","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Notice: <b>not</b> \"tormented in hell\" - not flogged by demons, <b>stabbed with a pitchfork</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tormented <b>in the presence of the Lamb</b> - what happens to <b>unrepentant wicked</b> coming into God's presence?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nadab and Abihu</b> - Aaron's sons enter tabernacle <b>drunk</b> to offer incense → <b>fire comes out from the presence of Yahweh</b> and consumes them</li><li class=\"d0\">Torah: coming into presence of God <b>as wicked, unrepentant, hardened in hatred</b> = horrible experience, described in <b>fire terms</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same Lamb: <b>144,000 have nothing to fear</b> - for these it's profoundly fearsome</li><li class=\"d0\">Why? Not because he hates them - <b>because they hate him</b></li></ul>"},{"t":735.08,"lv":3,"h":"Consuming fire: purified or consumed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hebrews: \"our God is a consuming fire\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Prophets use fire two ways - approach God, enter <b>fire of his holiness</b>:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>purified</b>: none of us arrive pure; metal <b>refined</b>, impurities burned off, <b>pure precious metal</b> left</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>consumed</b>: if all we are is impurities</li><li class=\"d0\">Same imagery here - recall first angel: <b>\"Get ready, God's coming\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Promise for some; <b>really bad</b> for others</li><li class=\"d0\">John isn't *seeing* it happen - an <b>angel proclaiming it as a warning</b>, before it happens</li></ul>"},{"t":818.24,"lv":3,"h":"A daily warning to the fence-sitters","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Like the other angels: not one thing on one future day - <b>a thing for every day</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John asks readers: <b>\"how much have you sold out?\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Many readers striving and <b>suffering</b>; others <b>straddling the fence</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>one foot in Roman system, one in the church</b> - \"sometimes maybe they say Christian, sometimes didn't\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Warning addressed to them: have you been <b>participant</b>? <b>Mark = participating in commerce, day-to-day things</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Given as warning because <b>it's not too late</b> if you're hearing it</li></ul>"},{"t":913.15,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:11 - Smoke of their torment","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Smoke of torment ascends forever and ever</b>; <b>no rest day or night</b> for those who worship beast and image and receive the mark</li><li class=\"d0\">Verb <b>\"who worship\"</b> = participle, <b>present tense</b> - not \"those who worshipped\"</li><li class=\"d0\">not \"you did this, so you're doomed / now being punished\"</li><li class=\"d0\">even in torment they <b>continue to follow the beast's image</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Unrepentant evil</b> → as long as lack of repentance is ongoing, <b>so is the suffering</b></li></ul>"},{"t":992.23,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:12 - The patience of the saints","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Here is the patience of the saints\"</b> - introduces <b>why saints are able to be patient</b></li><li class=\"d0\">patient = think of the martyrs: <b>\"How long, O Lord?\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Defines <b>saints / holy ones</b> - word also used of angels: those who <b>keep the commandments of God</b> and <b>\"the faith of Jesus\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Faith of Jesus\" = horrible <b>punt</b> - Jesus had faith and they have the same faith?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>faith = better \"faithfulness\"</b> → faithfulness related to Christ; parallel to <b>\"follow the Lamb wherever he goes\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Commandments mentioned <b>first</b> - \"sorry to our Protestant friends\": <b>faith is not alone</b></li><li class=\"d0\">not \"keep commandments and have the right ideas in their heads\" - \"I take my digs once in a while\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Keeping commandments = being faithful to Christ</b>, and faithful to Christ = you will keep them - <b>can't have one without the other</b></li><li class=\"d0\">patient = literally <b>long-suffering</b>: remain faithful despite suffering</li></ul>"},{"t":1191.45,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:13 - Blessed are the dead in the Lord","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Voice from heaven: \"Write, blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from now on\"</b> - \"Yes,\" says the <b>Spirit</b> - <b>rest from labors</b>, <b>works follow them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not distant future: <b>\"from now on\"</b> = from John's vision, really from <b>Christ's resurrection</b> - \"decades, but not that long\"</li><li class=\"d0\">This is <b>why saints can endure suffering</b> and stay faithful</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ends</b>: suffering, pain, sin, weakness, struggling - \"that dies, that's over\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Endures</b>: love shared, goodness, peace, <b>the person they became in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Blessed <b>no matter how they died</b> - tortured by Romans or old age in sleep, old or young</li></ul>"},{"t":1356.38,"lv":3,"h":"Radical: blessing in the ancient world","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ancient world: blessed = <b>long life, no bad things</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Aristotle</b>, <i>Nicomachean</i> and <i>Eudemian Ethics</i> - how to live a <b>happy life</b>, is it in your power? <b>fortune</b> vs <b>virtue</b></li><li class=\"d0\">died young, <b>tortured to death</b>, lived in poverty = <b>not blessed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pagan comparison: tortured <b>pagan Syrian</b> told to deny <b>Baal</b>, worship <b>Jupiter</b> → \"sure, no skin off my nose, probably the same dude anyway\" - not <b>long-suffering</b> like Christians</li><li class=\"d0\">Worst thing in this life = <b>a horrible death</b> - if that becomes <b>hope instead of fear</b>, you're truly blessed, <b>nothing to fear</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Origin of <b>\"no one can harm the righteous man\"</b> - kill him and you only end the bad, <b>all the good follows him</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1491.87,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:14 - One like the Son of Man on a cloud","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>White cloud</b>, one <b>like the Son of Man</b>, <b>golden crown</b>, <b>sharp sickle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Imagery from <b>Daniel</b> (more detail when we loop around) - \"kind of a <b>remix of the enthronement of Baal</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Daniel sees <b>Ancient of Days</b>, then <b>one like a son of man</b> = originally \"someone who looks human\", riding <b>clouds</b>, given <b>authority and power</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Is this a new sign? \"No, not yet\" - <b>coming up to the end</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Cloud rider\"</b> = a title of <b>Baal</b>, storm god - symbol of <b>divinity and power</b></li><li class=\"d0\">applied to <b>Yahweh</b> in several Psalms - read at <b>Vespers</b>: <b>\"walks upon the wings of the wind, makes the clouds his chariot\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Juxtaposed in Daniel: <b>looks human</b> but <b>rides the clouds</b> = mark of divinity</li></ul>"},{"t":1622.28,"lv":3,"h":"Son of Man: Messiah and Judge","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Second Temple, pre-Christian Jewish literature: <b>apocalyptic Son of Man</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Enoch</b> (3rd c. BC) connects him to <b>Messiah</b> - <b>divine Messiah</b> coming on clouds to <b>judge</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ uses <b>\"Son of Man\"</b> for himself all over, esp. <b>Matthew</b> - connecting himself to this figure</li><li class=\"d0\">Matthew/Mark: <b>\"when the Son of Man comes on the clouds with his holy angels to judge\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">To the <b>high priest</b>: \"Are you the Son of God?\" → <b>\"henceforth you will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"henceforth\" = \"this is how next time you see me\" - high priest: <b>\"we don't need any more witnesses, he blasphemed\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ clear to original Jewish readers: <b>this is Christ</b>, image of <b>Last Judgment</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1732.22,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:15-16 - Sickle and the harvest of the earth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sickle</b> = used at <b>harvest</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ on last judgment, esp. <b>Matthew</b>: <b>wheat and weeds</b>, <b>wheat and chaff</b> - <b>harvest and separating</b></li><li class=\"d0\">audience <b>subsistence farmers</b> - helpful metaphor; John picks it up</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ coming with sickle to <b>judge = separate out</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Another angel out of the temple</b>: \"Thrust in your sickle and reap, <b>the harvest of the earth is ripe</b>\" → the earth was reaped</li><li class=\"d0\">Which temple? Back to <b>heavenly sanctuary</b> - \"we've gone back to heaven\" (recall angel in midst of heaven)</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ's image: for a time <b>wheat and weeds grow together</b> - pulling weeds might <b>kill the wheat</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Then <b>harvest</b>, separated out</li><li class=\"d0\">Same in John: people <b>marked by God</b> and <b>mark of the beast</b> living together; things not going well for God's marked</li><li class=\"d0\">Now's the time \"things are going to be <b>set right</b>\" - <b>harvest begins</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1867.4,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:17-18 - Vine of the earth, ripe grapes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Another angel out of temple</b> with sharp sickle; <b>another from the altar, power over fire</b>: \"gather the clusters of <b>the vine of the earth</b>, for her grapes are <b>fully ripe</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Source of the title <b><i>Grapes of Wrath</i></b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Time known only to God</b> when judgment happens</li><li class=\"d0\">God gives <b>time for repentance</b> - wills <b>none should perish</b> - but <b>won't let evil go on forever</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Seen in: <b>whole world</b> (final judgment, Christ's return), <b>a nation or people group</b>, <b>an individual</b></li><li class=\"d0\">when <b>need to end evil outweighs more time to repent</b> → person leaves this world; nation judged; earth set right</li></ul>"},{"t":1926.24,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: why is wrath always wine?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: why is wrath always related to <b>wine</b> - drunk on power? drunkenness?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Unmingled wine</b> = no water: \"straight, pure, biting, burning, caustic\" - \"take a shot of whiskey\"</li><li class=\"d0\">ancient world: wine main drink, always <b>cut</b> with water → so potent it's \"almost like <b>poison</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>burning</b> element</li><li class=\"d0\">Hebrew idiom: wine = <b>\"blood of grapes\"</b> → blood connection too</li></ul>"},{"t":2037.05,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 14:19-20 - The great winepress","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Angel gathers the vine → <b>great winepress of the wrath of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Battle Hymn of the Republic</b> - \"not talking about the Union Army\" (\"not pro-Confederate even though I live in Louisiana\") - <b>vintage where grapes of wrath are stored</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Winepress trampled <b>outside the city</b>, <b>blood up to horses' bridles for 1,600 furlongs</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Orthodox Study Bible</b> notes: <b>184 miles</b>, \"give or take\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not exact measure - idea: <b>it's a lot</b>, <b>a torrent</b>, not a trickle</li></ul>"},{"t":2139.09,"lv":3,"h":"Sacrificial imagery","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: just saying \"you'll get squished\"? → actually <b>sacrificial imagery</b> - why John invoked <b>the temple in heaven</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Temple: constant <b>animal sacrifices</b>, blood drained and disposed of - <b>big gutters full of blood</b>, awful all the time; the <b>smell</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Happy to be a <b>priest of the new covenant</b> - I don't have to butcher animals\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wine press of God's wrath pouring blood</b> = sacrificial imagery applied to judgment</li><li class=\"d0\">Developed again in <b>next cycle</b>; <b>new cycle starts chapter 15</b> - another <b>set of seven</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2267.61,"lv":2,"h":"Day of the Lord: the sacrificial banquet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">OT prophets, <b>day of Yahweh</b>: Lord <b>preparing his sacrifice</b></li><li class=\"d0\">enemy <b>armies and their horses slaughtered</b>, offered as <b>food to vultures, buzzards, beasts</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God's <b>banquet for the scavenger / unclean animals</b> = sacrificial banquet of all his enemies</li><li class=\"d0\">John drops <b>first beginning of that image</b> here - develops it at <b>end of next cycle</b>; \"won't tease anymore\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2373.23,"lv":3,"h":"Inversion: evil turned into life-giving sacrifice","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Inversion image common elsewhere: <b>God smashing heads of Leviathan</b>, giving it as <b>food to the Ethiopians</b> (can't recall: Psalms or Isaiah)</li><li class=\"d0\">takes the enemy = <b>chaos, death, destruction</b> - not only <b>defeats</b> it but gives it as <b>nourishment to his creation</b>, <b>brings life out of it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">True of <b>all the wickedness in the world</b>: come to fruition → God <b>turns it into a sacrifice</b>, something that <b>gives life</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Stopping at <b>end of a chapter</b>, about to begin another cycle</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: <b>Revelation 15</b> - a new cycle of seven begins"});
